        "original_id": "2531d00a-8d75-5dfd-9846-ef3fa806d60e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vilayat Khan, Ravi Shankar, Ali Akbar Khan, Nikhil Banerjee, Imrat Khan, Baba Allauddin Khan, Enayat Khan\n- Organizations: Rajiv Gandhi National University of Law\n- Places: Patiala, Punjab, India, the West\n- Topics: Indian Classical Music, sitar, legal education\n\nFacts:\n- Vilayat Khan, along with Ravi Shankar, Ali Akbar Khan, Nikhil Banerjee, and his younger brother Imrat Khan, helped introduce Indian Classical Music to the West.\n- Nikhil Banerjee was a student of Baba Allauddin Khan.\n- Nikhil Banerjee was known for technical virtuosity and clinical execution.\n- Enayat Khan was the father of Vilayat Khan.\n- Vilayat Khan was one of the topmost sitar players of the postwar period.\n- Rajiv Gandhi National University of Law is a National Law University located in Patiala, Punjab, India.",
